{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2962","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2962","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2962\",\"parent_revision\":\"33b3d401edd53f3fd6ea5fa69b08489f6e62533e\",\"root_revision\":\"f9610b2ace89a0ac05d19425ebf7d4cbd8dee13839fa50d5e24b08770558c77f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-18\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\noperations._build_sections_from_yaml_item (backlog_core/operations.py) is used by view_item's YAML-only fallback path (no rendered GitHub body available) and returns section metadata keyed by the raw internal storage key (e.g. \\\"rt_ica\\\", \\\"unknown__decision\\\") instead of the human-readable display title (e.g. \\\"RT-ICA\\\", \\\"Decision\\\") that other code paths already use via rendering.section_display_title().\\n\\nWhere observed: reproducible on unmodified main for canonical sections \u2014 groom an item into section \\\"RT-ICA\\\" with no linked GitHub issue/body, then call view_item; result.sections shows key \\\"rt_ica\\\", not \\\"RT-ICA\\\". Discovered while fixing #2956 (backlog_groom section-key duplication bug); that fix corrected _normalize_section_key to route custom section names through the same normalizer GitHub-body parsing uses, which extended this same pre-existing raw-key exposure to custom/unknown sections too (e.g. \\\"unknown__decision\\\" instead of \\\"Decision\\\").\\n\\nImpact: an agent calling backlog_view for an item that has never synced to GitHub sees internal storage keys in the sections dict instead of the section names it wrote \u2014 confusing but not data-lossy (content is intact under the correct, if unreadable, key).\\n\\n**Research first**: Fix likely: route _build_sections_from_yaml_item's per-key output through rendering.section_display_title(key, ...) before returning, matching the pattern _render_section_index already uses for the same data. Confirm no caller relies on the raw key as a dict key for programmatic re-lookup before changing the key shape.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **view_item yaml-fallback surfaces raw section storage keys instead of display titles** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Additional Occurrence\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-18T01:22:19.319677Z</sub>\\n\\nConfirmed via live MCP validation while fixing #2956: the raw-key exposure is not limited to\\n_build_sections_from_yaml_item. backlog_view(selector=..., include_content=True) on a local-only\\n(no GitHub body) item returned sections_index=\\\"## Sections\\\\n[0] unknown__files (1 entries)\\\\n\\\" \u2014\\nraw storage key, not the display title \\\"Files\\\". The include_content=False (compact/summary) call\\non the SAME item correctly showed \\\"[0] Files (1 entries)\\\" via _render_section_index(), which does\\ncall rendering.section_display_title(). So the include_content=True path builds its sections_index\\nfrom a different function that skips the display-title conversion \u2014 likely\\n_build_sections_index_from_body()/_build_sections_compact() operating on a body string built\\nwithout routing section keys through section_display_title() first. Needs its own root-cause trace\\nbefore fixing (not done as part of #2956 \u2014 out of scope for that PR per explicit instruction).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3a95fa35bd4b26d24b07c76300057cce9942ec2f9fa3cb547504287a482ad61b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgv-yg\"}"}